🔹 Program 12: Collection of Polymorphic Shape Pointers

📌 Description

This program demonstrates how multiple derived objects can be stored and processed through a common abstract base-class interface.

"std::unique_ptr<Shape>" is used to safely store objects of different derived classes.

The program uses "Rectangle" and "Circle" objects and calls their overridden functions through base-class pointers.

🎯 Concept Used

Polymorphic Processing, Abstract Classes, Virtual Functions and Smart Pointers

💡 Key Point

Different derived objects can be handled uniformly through a common base-class interface.
